// Focused view: Push Gateway with its direct neighbors only.

views {
  style element.tag = #frontend   { color blue }
  style element.tag = #backend    { color sky }
  style element.tag = #data       { color secondary }
  style element.tag = #adminPlane { color indigo }
  style element.tag = #federation { color green }

  view servicePush of velox.pushGateway {
    title "Services / Push Gateway"
    description '''
      Consumes the Kafka `push-notifications` topic and dispatches to APNs, FCM, and
      Web Push. Kept separate from Delivery to isolate third-party vendor dependencies.

      ---

      **APNs (Apple Push Notification service)** — Apple's delivery channel for iOS and macOS.
      Push Gateway connects via the APNs HTTP/2 API using a provider certificate or token auth.

      **FCM (Firebase Cloud Messaging)** — Google's push channel for Android and web.
      Push Gateway uses the FCM HTTP v1 API with OAuth 2.0 service account credentials.

      **Web Push / VAPID** — Browser push standard (RFC 8030 + RFC 8292). VAPID lets Push
      Gateway authenticate with browser push services without a vendor account.

      **Device token** — Platform-specific identifier registered by the mobile app with
      Identity at login. Push Gateway looks it up to address a specific device on APNs/FCM.

      **Silent push** — Push notification that wakes the app in the background without
      displaying a banner. Used to trigger MLS state sync on the device before a visible
      notification appears, so the decrypted preview is ready immediately.
    '''
    include *
    include -> velox.pushGateway ->
    autoLayout LeftRight 120 80
  }
}
